{"format":"telly-addicts-eps","v":1,"show":"Food and Drink","eps":[{"s":1,"e":1,"t":"Tom Kerridge - British Food","a":"2013-02-04","l":30,"d":"Michel and the show's drinks expert Kate Goodman are joined by chef Tom Kerridge to create the perfect roast. Restaurateur Oliver Peyton explains why he believes that British produce needs to be celebrated much more than it currently is."},{"s":1,"e":2,"t":"Mary Berry - Baking","a":"2013-02-11","l":30,"d":"Michel and Kate are joined by Mary Berry and they create the perfect afternoon tea. Food writer William Sitwell praises sliced white bread while Rachel Khoo is in Paris to celebrate the patisserie."},{"s":1,"e":3,"t":"Jun Tanaka - Street Food","a":"2013-02-18","l":30,"d":"Michel and Kate are joined by are joined by Jun Tunaka to make the perfect burger. Monica Galetti shares her secrets for getting children to eat healthily. William Sitwell talks about his problems with the street food phenomenon."},{"s":1,"e":4,"t":"Monica Galetti - Comfort Food","a":"2013-02-25","l":30,"d":"Michela and Kate are joined by Monica Galetti to create the perfect comfort meal, Michel mother's shepherd's pie. William Sitwell takes a look at the obsession for nostalgic food and journalist Matthew Fort celebrates the return of stodgy British puddings."},{"s":1,"e":5,"t":"Series 1, Episode 5","a":"1982-08-03","l":30,"d":"Michel Roux Jr and drinks expert Kate Goodman are joined by Welsh Italian chef Angela Hartnett as they create the perfect Italian ragu and pasta. Journalist and Italophile Matthew Fort bemoans the inauthenticity of his favourite food outside of its mother country, and Antonio Carluccio celebrates the qualities that make the real thing so good."},{"s":1,"e":6,"t":"Rachel Khoo - Entertaining","a":"2013-03-11","l":30,"d":"Culinary legend Michel Roux Jr and drinks expert Kate Goodman are joined by cook and food writer Rachel Khoo as they create the perfect luxury dish to impress your friends. Restaurateur Oliver Peyton tries a new food experience that leaves him cold and food blogger and supper club entrepreneur Kerstin Rodgers shares her secrets for a successful dinner party."},{"s":2,"e":1,"t":"Series 2, Episode 1","a":"1983-04-28","l":30,"d":"Chef Michel Roux Jr and drinks expert Kate Goodman return for another series. This looks at how to cook up food that will help everyone's bottom line. We throw £640 million worth of bread in the bin every year, so guest Mary Berry surprises Michel with an ingenious use for stale bread to create fish pie topping which he admits he'd never have thought of himself."},{"s":2,"e":2,"t":"Series 2, Episode 2","a":"1983-05-05","l":30,"d":"Tom Kerridge joins Michel in the kitchen for Cheap Feasts and creates a mouth-watering meal for just £2 a head. The cost of our food is going up - rising more than three times faster than the average worker's wage. Tom and Michel are determined to demonstrate that you can spend less and eat well without sacrificing flavour."},{"s":2,"e":3,"t":"Series 2, Episode 3","a":"1983-05-12","l":30,"d":"How we eat and drink changes to reflect the way we live. Half of British families struggle to share a meal more than three times a week and yet we crave the sense of togetherness sharing food gives us. Richard Corrigan joins Michel in the kitchen to cook up the ultimate sharing food, a hearty chicken and crayfish pie."},{"s":2,"e":4,"t":"Series 2, Episode 4","a":"1983-05-19","l":30,"d":"If you had to trace the origins of the food you have eaten today, could you? Knowing what is in our food is more important than ever before. Chef Genarro Contaldo joins Michel Roux Jr in the kitchen to create an authentically Italian dish from scratch - a sumptuous lasagne with focaccia."},{"s":2,"e":5,"t":"Series 2, Episode 5","a":"1983-05-26","l":30,"d":"Scottish chef Tony Singh joins Michel Roux Jr in the studio to prove that, even in winter, it's possible to eat well using seasonally available ingredients. He creates a seasonal feast of venison with haggis ravioli and argues that eating with the seasons is all about picking the best of the month's home-grown ingredients and cooking creatively!"},{"s":2,"e":6,"t":"Series 2, Episode 6","a":"1983-06-02","l":30,"d":"Gregg Wallace joins Michel in the kitchen and helps him create a mouth-watering meal in which meat is just the garnish - demonstrating that we can eat less meat without sacrificing flavour. Kate finds some fantastic white wine matches from Portugal, and chef Florence Knight shows how to cook a by-product of garlic you may never have heard of."},{"s":2,"e":7,"t":"Series 2, Episode 7","a":"1983-06-09","l":30,"d":"Ken Hom joins Michel in the kitchen and shows him how to create a delicious citrus-flavoured chicken dish in minutes. Kate picks three different Semillon wines from Australia to compliment Ken's stir fry and Michel creates a fruity pancake dessert that has everyone's mouths watering."},{"s":2,"e":8,"t":"Series 2, Episode 8","a":"1983-06-16","l":30,"d":"Angela Hartnett joins Michel Roux Jr in the kitchen and shows him how to create a pizza bianco using rich and creamy taleggio cheese. Kate Goodman picks three Italian reds that perfectly complement Angela's pizza, while Rachel Khoo argues the case for full-fat food, and Michel creates an indulgent chocolate and salted caramel dessert."},{"s":2,"e":9,"t":"Series 2, Episode 9","a":"1983-06-23","l":30,"d":"Monica Galetti joins Michel Roux Jr in the kitchen and shows him how to create a low-fat, low-carb, flavour-packed meal while Kate Goodman surprises them both with some tasty, healthy drinks using bitters. Journalist William Sitwell asks whether food intolerances are all in our mind and Michel makes a refreshing and mouthwatering tuna tartare."},{"s":2,"e":10,"t":"Series 2, Episode 10","a":"1983-06-30","l":30,"d":"Sat Bains joins Michel in the kitchen to demonstrate his take on a traditional bread and butter pudding. He uses cutting-edge culinary equipment to create a modern twist on this classic dish. Kate finds some fantastic dessert wines to go with Sat's unusual dish and Stefan Gates asks whether we should be eating meat that has been grown in a laboratory."},{"s":2,"e":11,"t":"Christmas Special"},{"s":3,"e":1,"t":"Series 3, Episode 1","a":"1994-03-08","l":30,"d":"Chef and pub landlord Tom Kerridge plays host to Britain's best cooks and chefs in a series highlighting all that is excellent in food and drink. Tom challenges the Hairy Bikers to come up with a speedy meal to rival his hearty and wholesome sausage and bean casserole.","img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/266874/5088793.jpg"},{"s":3,"e":2,"t":"Series 3, Episode 2","a":"1984-03-15","l":30,"d":"Michelin-starred chef Tom Kerridge is joined in the kitchen by MasterChef judge Monica Galetti - a chef who knows how to get maximum flavour with minimal fuss. They go head to head to come up with the best simple but spectacular recipe. Monica's perfectly tender, honey-glazed chicken versus Tom's simple but sophisticated celery soup with poached egg and soda bread.","img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/266874/5088794.jpg"},{"s":3,"e":3,"t":"Series 3, Episode 3","a":"1984-03-22","l":30,"d":"Michelin-starred pub landlord Tom Kerridge is back with a new episode of Food & Drink. Forget your pilaffs and paellas - tonight's show is all about the best of British food. Tom is joined by Hugh Fearnley-Whittingstall - a passionate champion of British dishes. He cooks a classic roast chicken to go up against Tom's great British stew and dumplings.","img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/266874/5088795.jpg"},{"s":3,"e":4,"t":"Series 3, Episode 4","a":"1984-03-29","l":30,"d":"Michelin-starred pub landlord Tom Kerridge is joined by Irish chef Richard Corrigan to go head to head and produce the best dish made from the unsung heroes of the British larder. Richard is a big fan of one of our least loved ingredients - offal.","img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/266874/5111761.jpg"},{"s":3,"e":5,"t":"Series 3, Episode 5","a":"1984-04-05","l":30,"d":"Michelin-starred chef and pub landlord Tom Kerridge is joined by Italian chef and restaurateur Angela Hartnett in an episode about how to make delicious, top-notch food on a budget. Angela brings along her dog Alfie for moral support in her cook-off with Tom to create the best value-for-money dish - her vanilla custard tart versus his beef and blue cheese risotto.","img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/266874/5111762.jpg"},{"s":3,"e":6,"t":"Series 3, Episode 6","a":"1984-04-12","l":30,"d":"Michelin-starred chef and pub landlord Tom Kerridge reveals how to reach the heady heights of happiness through healthy food. Award-winning Indian chef and one half of the Incredible Spice Men, Cyrus Todiwala joins Tom in the kitchen and is challenged to come up with an alternative take on a gut-busting curry to rival Tom's macho spice-crusted tuna salad.","img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/266874/5111763.jpg"},{"s":3,"e":7,"t":"Series 3, Episode 7","a":"1984-04-19","l":30,"d":"Michelin-starred chef and pub landlord Tom Kerridge challenges celebrated cook Ching He Huang to rustle up the perfect party food. Ching's chicken and mushroom pies and spicy salmon rice balls compete with Tom's chicken nuggets and carrot and pistachio baklava.","img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/266874/5111765.jpg"},{"s":4,"e":1,"t":"Series 4, Episode 1","a":"1984-10-25","l":30},{"s":4,"e":2,"t":"Series 4, Episode 2","a":"1984-11-01","l":30},{"s":4,"e":3,"t":"Series 4, Episode 3","a":"1984-11-08","l":30},{"s":4,"e":4,"t":"Series 4, Episode 4","a":"1984-11-15","l":30},{"s":4,"e":5,"t":"Series 4, Episode 5","a":"1984-11-22","l":30},{"s":4,"e":6,"t":"Series 4, Episode 6","a":"1984-11-29","l":30},{"s":4,"e":7,"t":"Series 4, Episode 7","a":"1984-12-06","l":30},{"s":4,"e":8,"t":"Series 4, Episode 8","a":"1984-12-13","l":30},{"s":4,"e":9,"t":"Christmas Special"},{"s":4,"e":10,"t":"S